0cf0473b-70da-4f0f-ad28-055b2791acd7	b16e8a96-c6f0-413c-9850-62315d2ff845	assistant	When students miss lectures or experience periods of absence, they remain responsible for keeping up with their academic work. According to the *Student Attendance and Leave Policy 2026* (page 1), student responsibilities during an absence include:\n\n* Obtaining lecture notes and learning materials.\n* Contacting lecturers regarding missed lessons.\n* Completing assignments within the published deadlines.\n* Reviewing announcements on the university learning management system.\n* Arranging to complete missed practical activities where permitted.\n\nAdditionally, students should inform their relevant lecturer or academic department when they are unable to attend scheduled sessions. If you need further assistance with attendance matters, you can contact your programme coordinator or the Student Services Department.	["c83c6ce1-f1be-4b71-9c66-c8f6f879aa97", "a7af1936-96d7-4b78-9502-e2db7553f837", "e577b579-dca8-443c-82f4-dc2d5890e544", "55238a43-61ed-42dc-a851-85249181e101", "e77e8ab5-3879-4b41-8c8b-4a65f28469bb"]	2026-11-06 10:08:14.239306+00
