access, account problems, campus network access and supported university systems. Library and Learning Centre: Access to study spaces, learning resources, borrowing services and research guidance. Borrowing periods and renewal rules are determined by the library's current procedures. Admissions Office: Application status, programme entry requirements and offer-related enquiries. Northstar University | Synthetic demonstration document Page 5 7. University Office Directory The following contact information is fictional and is included to test document search and question answering. The email addresses use the reserved .example domain and are not real mailboxes. Office Telephone Email Office hours General Enquiries +94 11 200 1000 info@northstar.example Mon-Fri, 8:00 AM-5:00 PM Admissions Office +94 11 200 1001 admissions@northstar.example Mon-Fri, 8:30 AM-4:30 PM Student Affairs +94 11 200 1002 studentaffairs@northstar.example Mon-Fri, 8:30 AM-4:30 PM IT Support +94 11 200 1003 itsupport@northstar.example Mon-Fri, 8:00 AM-5:00 PM Finance Office +94 11 200 1004 finance@northstar.example Mon-Fri, 8:30 AM-4:30 PM Examination Office +94 11 200 1005 examinations@northstar.example Mon-Fri, 8:30 AM-4:30 PM 8. General Student Questions Where should a prospective student ask about entry requirements? Contact the Admissions Office and identify the programme of interest. Who should be contacted about a payment that is not showing in the student account? Contact the Finance Office and provide the payment receipt through the university's approved communication process. Where should a student report a problem with a university account? Contact IT Support and provide a short description of the issue. Do not send passwords by email or share them with support staff. Who handles examination timetable and result enquiries? Contact the Examination Office and include the relevant module or examination details. Where can a student ask for general campus guidance? Contact Student Affairs or the General Enquiries desk. 9. Document Review and Information Accuracy University information can change. Students should consult the latest approved policy, announcement or official communication when information appears inconsistent. Where two documents conflict, the document owner or responsible university office should confirm which version applies. For a real knowledge management system, each uploaded document should have an owner, a review date, a publication status and, where appropriate, an effective date and expiry date. Superseded policies should be archived so that users are not given outdated guidance. End of demonstration handbook. Testing suggestions After uploading this PDF, try searching for: the annual tuition fee, the Admissions Office telephone number, the office responsible for examination enquiries, the sample academic integrity rules, and the IT Support email address. These questions help test text extraction and retrieval across different sections of the document.	[-0.0011517558,0.017644227,-0.014353105,0.0029401968,-0.0032152482,-0.018181099,0.0150165,0.050318174,-0.0043800464,-0.11026281,-0.026885744,0.0029769035,-0.008729783,0.022116402,0.015438161,-0.044463664,0.021517243,-0.032647364,0.018150887,-0.0163937,0.019496204,-0.011065187,-0.06143353,0.00036304147,-0.047903985,0.027784452,-0.009602184,-0.017811127,0.0033026254,0.21639186,-0.02555765,-0.0007711327,-0.0039343876,-0.038508937,-0.0027568033,-0.009793858,0.009986903,0.04516712,0.018832078,0.05391801,0.021304054,0.015763063,-0.055103436,0.011432446,0.010160109,0.017128706,-0.0041002003,0.0051696813,0.018436342,0.02466583,0.010572634,-0.011396985,0.0002429379,-0.026522327,-0.015493073,0.036627933,0.024352113,0.05068852,0.029033914,0.021663742,0.0067471503,-0.040050764,0.037057646,-0.007503427,0.022455368,-0.019381842,0.0013528712,-0.03134109,0.009093017,0.015166741,-0.0109236175,-0.019046357,-0.016595095,0.0015197659,0.046172537,-0.08840897,-0.05032297,0.0239237,-0.0071501685,0.021732