51173b2c-2e6a-4160-92b0-8f49b1b460e2	a632203b-4d55-4714-aca6-42ad61aae9ee	c0e954d5-1e9f-4d10-8493-3553c873c204	0	1	Northstar University | Student Services Page 1 NORTHSTAR UNIVERSITY Student Attendance and Leave Policy 2026 Document Category: Student Services Document Type: University Policy Academic Year: 2026 1. Introduction Northstar University recognises regular class attendance as an important part of academic progress. Students are expected to attend scheduled lectures, practical sessions, laboratory activities, tutorials, and other academic activities included in their programmes. 2. Attendance Requirements All registered students are expected to maintain regular attendance throughout each academic semester. • Students should attend all scheduled academic sessions. • Attendance will be recorded by the relevant academic department. • Students must arrive on time for lectures and practical sessions. • Students should inform the relevant lecturer or academic department when they are unable to attend. • Attendance records may be considered during academic progress reviews. 3. Absence Due to Medical Reasons Students who cannot attend academic activities due to illness or medical circumstances should notify their academic department as soon as reasonably possible. Where required, students may be asked to submit supporting medical documentation issued by a recognised medical practitioner or healthcare institution. The academic department will review submitted documentation according to university procedures. 4. Leave Application Procedure Students requesting planned leave should follow these steps: 1. Contact the relevant academic department. 2. Explain the reason for the requested absence. 3. Provide the expected dates of absence. 4. Submit supporting documents where applicable. 5. Wait for confirmation from the responsible university officer. Submitting a leave request does not automatically mean that the request has been approved. 5. Academic Responsibilities During Absence Students remain responsible for keeping up with their academic work during periods of absence. • Obtain lecture notes and learning materials. • Contact lecturers regarding missed lessons. • Complete assignments within the published deadlines. • Review announcements on the university learning management system. Northstar University | Student Services Page 2 • Arrange to complete missed practical activities where permitted. 6. Attendance Records The relevant academic department is responsible for maintaining student attendance records. Students who believe their attendance records contain errors should contact the department and provide relevant information for verification. Any correction will be subject to review and approval by the authorised academic staff. 7. Special Circumstances Requests involving exceptional personal, medical, or other circumstances may be reviewed individually. The university may request additional information before making a decision. 8. Student Support Students who require assistance with attendance matters should contact their programme coordinator or the Student Services Department. Department: Student Services Institution: Northstar University Document Year: 2026 9. Policy Review This document is intended as a sample university policy for Knowledge Hub testing. Official attendance requirements should be confirmed against the university's approved academic regulations. End of Document Sample document for software testing. It is not an official Northstar University policy.	[0.020148816,0.049121473,-0.010480627,-0.0036983807,-0.024997976,0.012999647,-0.046891358,0.0748943,-0.0071037943,-0.08330231,0.015275135,0.013950917,0.019296896,0.030306559,0.021065937,-0.042913564,-0.0011713112,-0.04053177,0.01956488,-0.012675711,0.03741126,-0.007206557,-0.0048041684,0.036430374,-0.020637976,-0.056775052,0.009179873,-0.043056253,-0.036183827,0.19950262,-0.014133715,-0.030227391,0.01695859,-0.0116935745,0.016829195,0.0055215703,-0.0023174048